1: #  ------------------------------------------------------------ pvrrenderexit (#NNN)
2: #  dev_pvr.c's renderer ended the emulator (fatal() + exit(1)) on a polygon header whose list word 1 sets bit 26 (Z-write disable).
3: #  Now such a polygon goes through the same depth test and rasterization as any other and only its depth store is skipped, in both
4: #  rasterizers, and every render clears the flag first.  The rung-3 witness (regress/artifacts/pvrrenderexit/witness_20261104/) is
5: #  NOT run here; this is its detector: 164 rows -- the witness's nine plus fifty-eight render sessions whose pixels are read back
6: #  through the linear VRAM window (the depth-test cells of both rasterizers, two renders in one session, the x-range bound at both
7: #  screen edges, the equal-depth edge, repair 2's y range, span end and start, swap and bit-26 decode neighbours, repair 3's class
8: #  closure -- the swap's other edges and body, reversed spans across both edges, the left clause's compares at their edge, a Z-off
9: #  polygon at equal depth, the decode's `== 1` and wider masks, and a Z-OFF TWIN of every single-layer geometry session and of the
10: #  swap-body session -- repair 4's half-pixel edges of simpleline's position compares and the swap body's far end, and repair 5's
11: #  swap body read from above and span starts at a negative x, and repair 7's renders with a non-zero frame base or a non-zero
12: #  PALETTE_CFG and first PALETTE register, each with its Z-off twin).  Needs only the binary: -E dreamcast with a 4-byte dummy
13: #  image at 0x8c010000, 1-4 s (r7_20261105/base164/: 4.0 s; table7/probe_base.out: 1.4 s).  (Corrected 2026-11-05, repair 3: this
14: #  said 'fifteen render sessions' -- repair 2 made sixteen -- and 'about half a second', which held for the 51-row probe; the
15: #  68-row probe took ~90 s, because one session's input passed the 4100-byte debugger stdin cap and waited out its timeout --
16: #  r3_20261105/PVR3_NOTE.md.  The probe now refuses such a session before running that session.)  It sits here rather than in
17: #  gate_sh_rounding.sh with the other dreamcast probes only because that file carried another session's uncommitted work when it
18: #  landed.  Test-variant tables: regress/artifacts/pvrrenderexit/det_20261104/table1/ (the 51-row probe), r2_20261105/table2/ (the
19: #  68-row probe), r3_20261105/table3/ (the 128-row probe: 129 of its 130 predictions hit; the miss was a Z-off twin left out of one
20: #  prediction, r3_20261105/PRETABLE_3.errata.md), r4_20261105/table4/ (the 140-row probe: all 148 of its predictions hit -- B2t's
